In this experiment, I worked with two different LLM providers, Gemini and Ollama. The main idea was to make one Python program that can work with different AI models. I created a common class for the providers and separate classes for Gemini and Ollama. I also added an option to select which provider I wanted to use. After selecting the provider, I could enter a prompt and get a response from the model. I also created a test file to check whether the program was working correctly. This experiment helped me understand how different AI models can be connected to the same application and how abstraction is used in Python.
